(4272645, 615186, 86794, '<td valign="top">Thanks for your votes and comments, everybody!<br/> <br/>I agree that I should have included the entire container in this shot.  <br/> <br/>While walking on the balcony surrounding my college''s library,  I leaned over the handrail and saw the book-filled dumpster from pretty much the same point of view you see in my photo.<br/>This was on the last day of the submission period for this challenge and by the time my model showed up, the sun was already beginning to set (stupid daylight wastings time). The pressure kept me from concentrating, so this was the best shot I ended up with.  Still work though, I think.<br/> <br/>I''m happy to give those books some final appreciation.  Seems like such a waste to toss them, doesn''t it?  They were mostly outdated physics textbooks, but still.<br/> <br/>I know what you guys mean about me winning with my very first entry.  Sorry!<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2007-11-28 02:47:27.</i></td>', 'Thanks for your votes and comments, everybody! I agree that I should have included the entire container in this shot.   While walking on the balcony surrounding my college''s library,  I leaned over the handrail and saw the book-filled dumpster from pretty much the same point of view you see in my photo.This was on the last day of the submission period for this challenge and by the time my model showed up, the sun was already beginning to set (stupid daylight wastings time). The pressure kept me from concentrating, so this was the best shot I ended up with.  Still work though, I think. I''m happy to give those books some final appreciation.  Seems like such a waste to toss them, doesn''t it?  They were mostly outdated physics textbooks, but still. I know what you guys mean about me winning with my very first entry.  Sorry!', '2007-11-28 02:04:04.000000', '2007-11-28 02:47:27.000000', 0),
